WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.780
In 1994, San Francisco
extended rent control to small,

2
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.580
older rental buildings.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:11.640
Covered tenants became nearly 20 percent
more likely to stay at their address.

4
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.490
Sounds like a clear win.

5
00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:17.270
So why do economists still
argue about rent control?

6
00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:21.460
What really happens when a government
makes something cheaper by law?

7
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.260
In this mission, you'll draw a
price ceiling below equilibrium,

8
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.280
and see what happens to quantity
demanded and quantity supplied.

9
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.000
Then you'll find out why
a ceiling on a monopoly

10
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.180
can work very differently.

11
00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.150
Your mission: find out what
happens when a government

12
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:39.160
makes something cheaper by law.
